From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jackie Han <jackie.han@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "firmware: qcom: scm: Disable SDI and write no dump to dump mode"

Commit 79cb2cb8d89b ("firmware: qcom: scm: Disable SDI and write no dump
to dump mode") made qcom_scm_probe() always call
qcom_scm_set_download_mode() and call qcom_scm_disable_sdi() whenever
download mode is disabled, regardless of the "qcom,sdi-enabled" DT
property.

On ipq40xx (legacy SMC convention) this makes warm resets unreliable:
the board either crashes a few seconds after boot or hangs at
"Starting kernel". Only set the download mode when it is requested and
only disable SDI when the DT says it is enabled by default, as before
79cb2cb8d89b.

The reason why these calls break warm reset on ipq40xx is not known.
This is an OpenWrt-local workaround for ipq40xx and not meant for
mainline in this form.

Fixes: 79cb2cb8d89b ("firmware: qcom: scm: Disable SDI and write no dump to dump mode")
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/22807
Signed-off-by: Jackie Han <jackie.han@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2559,12 +2559,13 @@ static int qcom_scm_probe(struct platfor
 	 * will cause the boot stages to enter download mode, unless
 	 * disabled below by a clean shutdown/reboot.
 	 */
-	qcom_scm_set_download_mode(download_mode);
+	if (download_mode)
+		qcom_scm_set_download_mode(download_mode);
 
 	/*
 	 * Disable SDI if indicated by DT that it is enabled by default.
 	 */
-	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,sdi-enabled") || !download_mode)
+	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,sdi-enabled"))
 		qcom_scm_disable_sdi();
 
 	/*
